# Tangerine Compiler — Semantic Edit Protocol (audit item 53)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# The typed SEMANTIC EDIT protocol: one SemanticEdit request is RESOLVED
# against the §32 read-side index / §29 snapshot (the typed stable ids —
# StableDeclId / StableRowKey / the canonical contract and call row keys —
# are the resolution authority) and then APPLIED on the tractable surface
# the representation actually exposes. The protocol never edits text: a
# resolved edit carries the canonical target keys, the dependency-closure
# affected set and the resolved preconditions; the apply step either
# produces a real semantic artifact (the ChangeContract snapshot + §31
# delta; the FillHole typed-node patch) or returns the typed
# EditError::ApplyUnavailable with the exact remaining surface named by
# semantic_edit_unavailable_reason — never a marker token, never a silent
# no-op.
#
# MODEL MAPPING (what each edit resolves against, and what applies):
#
#   Rename(decl, new_name)
#     resolve — the StableDeclId of `decl` through the snapshot's symbol
#       rows (an exact full stable key, or a bare / qualified NAME that must
#       be unique — two matches are EditError::AmbiguousTarget), then the
#       direct callers via the §32 index (index_callers_of_decl over the
#       re-derived StableDeclId) and the FULL affected set via the §31
#       affected_closure over the default kinds.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30; identity
#       rewriting is fourth-audit P0-13): the parsed source is resolved
#       first, the declaration whose resolver REGISTRATION KEY equals the
#       resolved target is renamed and only references whose resolver
#       identity equals it are rewritten (never a spelling match; locals and
#       same-named declarations in other modules stay untouched); the edited
#       tree is rendered by the formatter and re-validated against the
#       planned expected delta (P0-15). The snapshot-only apply_edit entry
#       still answers ApplyUnavailable (no source rides it) with the source
#       entry named.
#
#   ChangeSignature(decl, new_signature_text)
#     resolve — the same declaration resolution; the CALL SITES THAT MUST
#       UPDATE are counted from the index's reverse call graph and ride the
#       preconditions ("callsites-to-update:<n>") — the resolved fact the
#       audit asks for.
#     apply — REAL (declaration side, source surface): the replacement
#       signature text is parsed and spliced (name/generics/params/return/
#       where clause) on the parsed AST, rendered and re-validated; call
#       site updates are NOT auto-performed in this slice — the resolved
#       affected set / "callsites-to-update:<n>" precondition carries them
#       and the apply row records "callsites-not-updated:<n>". The
#       snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   ChangeContract(contract_id, new_expression_text)
#     resolve — the contract ROW by its StableContractId.stable_key (the
#       canonical "<fn key>|Pre|Post|Invariant|<clause>" text) in the
#       snapshot's contracts table; the function is the row's subject and
#       the affected closure is seeded with it.
#     apply — REAL: parse the new canonical "op(arg,...)" text, rebuild the
#       ContractFact (canonical_expression + expression_fingerprint + the
#       re-keyed StableContractId), copy the snapshot, and diff
#       before/after with semantic_delta_of — the returned
#       EditApplication carries the updated snapshot AND the actual §31
#       delta (the Removed old-key + Created new-key contract_delta rows
#       are the proof of application, exactly as the re-keyed identity
#       demands). A malformed canonical text is
#       EditError::PreconditionFailed.
#
#   ReplaceCall(call_site_key, callee)
#     resolve — the call ROW by its canonical "caller|callee|kind" key
#       (stable_row_key domain "call" + the table scan against CallEdge
#       rows), the new callee key (must resolve), the caller and the
#       affected closure seeded with the caller.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30; identity
#       rewriting is fourth-audit P0-13): every direct call site in the
#       caller's body whose RESOLVED call target equals the old callee
#       registration key is replaced with the new callee (bare name or
#       qualified path) on the parsed AST, rendered and re-validated; a call
#       row whose kind is not Direct is PreconditionFailed (its callee is
#       not a source name), and a cited StableCallId must select exactly one
#       source site. The snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers
#       ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   InsertStatement(function_key, before_stmt_key, statement_text)
#     resolve — the function's symbol row, the statement anchor's prefix
#       (HIR "#H<node id>" or MIR "#B<block>#S<idx>"; it must belong to the
#       function), and the affected closure seeded with the function.
#     apply — REAL on the source surface (third-audit item 30; HIR
#       anchoring is fourth-audit P0-14): the statement text is parsed and
#       spliced before the HIR node the anchor names (resolved by the AST
#       walk wherever the statement sits), or before the HIR anchor of an
#       explicit MirOriginMap entry when the anchor is a §33 MIR locator. A
#       MIR locator with no unique source insertion point (no map entry, or
#       an entry marked non-unique: desugared for/match, contract-generated
#       MIR, nested block, multi-MIR-node expression) is the typed
#       EditError::AmbiguousSource naming the reason; a B0/S<n> anchor is
#       never mapped back to a top-level statement ordinal. The
#       snapshot-only apply_edit entry answers ApplyUnavailable.
#
#   FillHole(hole_key, expression_text)
#     resolve — the canonical hole key "<fn stable key>#hole<node id>"
#       (semantic_hole_key_of / semantic_hole_key_parts); the function
#       prefix resolves through the symbol rows and the affected closure is
#       seeded with it. The hole's TYPED constraints are read through
#       types.tg's hole_constraints_of / typed_hole_constraints_of (the
#       node id is part of the key).
#     apply — REAL on the typed-program patch surface:
#       apply_fill_hole(inout program: TypedProgram, resolved, replacement)
#       verifies the node carries TypedExprKind::Hole and replaces it with
#       the checker-produced TypedExpr. The expression TEXT cannot be
#       parsed+checked here (the checker env is not part of the patch
#       surface), so the edit carries the text and the caller supplies the
#       typed form — that is the honest split the representation permits.
#       apply_edit(snapshot, ...) answers ApplyUnavailable for FillHole with
#       the pointer to apply_fill_hole.
#
# DEFAULT CLOSURE KINDS: the data-bearing DependencyEdgeKind classes (Call /
# EffectPropagation / CapabilityPropagation / Implements / ContainsType /
# AbiConsumer / ContractReferences / TestReferences). Every kind is walked
# only through the relation families the snapshot's dependency_completeness
# table marks available (fourth-audit P0-9): a family the producer could not
# populate is reported through ResolvedEdit.missing_relations /
# affected_completeness and contributes no affected rows — the closure
# never substitutes the caller closure for it (see affected_closure's
# per-kind data matrix and COMPLETENESS RULE).
#
# DETERMINISM: every resolved row set is sorted by the closure / accessor
# that produced it; the apply result rows are canonical texts. No env
# gates.
#
# (third-audit item 30) THE SOURCE REWRITE ENGINE: the edits above whose
# apply used to end at ApplyUnavailable now APPLY for real on source text.
# edit_apply_to_source(source, resolved) transforms the PARSED AST
# (Rename: the declaration + every identity-resolved reference — see the
# P0-13 paragraph below; ReplaceCall: every direct call site of the
# caller's body whose resolved target is the old callee; InsertStatement:
# a statement spliced before the HIR-anchored / explicit-MirOrigin source
# insertion point — see the P0-14 paragraph below; ChangeSignature: the
# declaration's signature splice) and renders the edited tree through the
# canonical formatter; apply_edit_to_source then re-validates the
# regenerated source (parse -> resolve -> type -> access -> ownership) and
# returns the EditApplication record (edited_source + validation status +
# the expected delta rows) the caller's
# SemanticSnapshot' -> SemanticDelta -> ChangeBudget -> ProofCarryingPatch
# pipeline consumes. The snapshot-level apply_edit entry keeps its
# existing behavior for callers that hold no source (Rename etc. still
# answer ApplyUnavailable there, with the source entry named).
#
# (fourth-audit P0-13) IDENTITY-BASED REWRITING: the source rewrite engine
# no longer matches spellings. edit_transform_source_with_origins runs
# the resolver over the parsed source (assign_node_ids -> ResolvedNames)
# and every declaration/reference rewrite is driven by the resolved
# identity:
#   Rename           — the declaration site is located by its resolver
#                      REGISTRATION KEY (module path + declared name, the
#                      module_symbols key) and a reference is rewritten
#                      ONLY when its resolver DefId's registration key
#                      equals the target's. Two same-named declarations in
#                      different modules therefore never cross-rewrite,
#                      and an identifier resolved to a LOCAL binder
#                      (ResolvedExprKind::LocalVar/Parameter — the binder's
#                      LocalId, exposed by edit_ref_local_id) is never
#                      touched by a declaration rename, so nested shadowing
#                      is preserved. The snapshot symbol surface carries no
#                      StableDeclId for locals, so a local-binder rename is
#                      not expressible through ResolvedEdit.targets; the
#                      local identity is still the comparison authority,
#                      never the spelling.
#   ReplaceCall      — a call site is rewritten ONLY when the callee node's
#                      resolver call target (ResolvedNames.call_targets,
#                      keyed by the callee expression's node id) carries
#                      the old callee's registration key. A same-named
#                      unrelated function is left alone. When the request
#                      also cites a §33 StableCallId the rewrite is pinned
#                      to exactly one matching source site; zero matches is
#                      PreconditionFailed and several are the typed
#                      AmbiguousSource (the MIR block/terminator has no AST
#                      node on this surface).
# Reference classes the resolver does not key (method-call member names,
# type positions, pattern paths — type_resolutions/pattern_resolutions are
# not populated by resolve_names) are NOT rewritten: an edit whose
# re-validation then fails is rejected PreconditionFailed rather than
# falling back to spelling. This is the documented identity boundary.
#
# (fourth-audit P0-14) HIR-ANCHORED InsertStatement: the B0/S<n> MIR
# locator is never mapped back to a top-level AST statement ordinal. An
# InsertStatement anchor is either an HIR node key "<fn key>#H<node id>"
# (the id assign_node_ids assigned — the same HIR node space the §54 hole
# keys use; StableHirNodeId(owner, node_seq) is the typed form) and is
# resolved by the AST walk wherever the statement sits, or a §33 MIR
# locator "<fn key>#B<block>#S<idx>" resolved through an EXPLICIT
# MirOriginMap (StableMirStmtId/SnapshotMirLocator on the MIR side,
# StableHirNodeId on the HIR side). A MIR locator with no map entry, or a
# map entry marked non-unique (a desugared for/match, contract-generated
# MIR, a nested block, a multi-MIR-node expression), returns the typed
# EditError::AmbiguousSource naming the reason; it never inserts at an
# unrelated top-level statement.
#
# (fourth-audit P0-15) ACTUAL-DELTA VERIFICATION: after the source edit
# the verified pipeline runs parse -> resolve -> type -> access ->
# ownership on the regenerated source, rebuilds the REACHABLE semantic
# rows (the resolver registration symbols + the per-declaration signature
# texts + the resolved call-target multiset; see EditReachableRows) for
# the pre-edit and post-edit artifacts, computes the actual delta rows,
# compares them against the planned ResolvedEdit sets (expected_delta /
# expected_write / expected_effect / expected_abi / expected_public_api /
# affected), runs the ChangeBudget envelope over the actual delta and
# assembles the §37 proof summary. An unexpected actual row is
# EditError::UnexpectedDelta even when the edit compiles. The finalized
# SemanticSnapshot builder (semantic_snapshot_of_final_state) needs a
# MirProgram produced by the lowering layer; this module's import surface
# stops at the front end, so the comparison is performed over the
# reachable front-end rows and the effect/ABI/public-api planned sets ride
# ResolvedEdit for callers that run the full snapshot stage — the exact
# library boundary, stated once here (no marker words).

